// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// use this to manage Sarah's commentary and make it work across scenarios
// TOC: There are no TOC entries and this is ordered|nokeep:  this means the next page will be read each time it is opened
// The default page text entries are for goal == goalCloseGate
// Note that the "visible" directives may change during the game, so pages with visibility rules might show out of order

Language English
Debug Off

BOOK SarahPatter Ordered No Keep
	Triggered By @Sarah If foundSarah And Not ritual

	Page Color1
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You don't remember
			me or what happened 10 years ago. I am your little sister.
			
			<<I will tell you everything you need to know, but first I must
			tell you that our cousin, Mathias, will open a gate
			tonight. You must stop him. If you cannot stop him, you will
			need to find a way to close that gate.>>
		"""

		If goal = goalFeedGate Then Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You don't remember
			me or what happened 10 years ago. I am your little sister.
			
			<<I will tell you everything you need to know, but first I must
			tell you that our cousin, Mathias, will open a gate
			tonight. You must stop him. If that gate opens, evil could destroy
			the world.>>
		"""
	End Page Color1

	Page Color2
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The people in this
			town worship a darker god than most. They want to bring their god
			to Earth. 10 years ago, Our father, Elias, cast a ritual to summon It. He
			opened a gate using my body. The power it possessed was breathtaking
			and I could do nothing to stop it. Somehow, Father summoned local
			church members through the gate to protect it, even after he
			was dead. As the gate, I could feel people and monsters
			approaching and passing through me from the either side.>>
		"""
	End Page Color2

	Page PeterIsDead
		Visible If peterIsDead
		
		Text """
			Sarah leans in and whispers into {c:EventChosenInvestigator}'s
			ear. She is visibly upset.
			
			<<I didn't know Uncle Peter was killed
			that night. Everyone thought he and Father ran off
			together after Uncle Peter put a stop to the ritual.>>
			
			She chokes up momentarily and a single tear runs down her right
			cheek. She takes a breath and shakes it off. <<Tears are for
			later.>>
			
			She's quiet for a moment, then says, <<Now
			I know what really happened. And it will not happen again.>>
		"""
	End Page PeterIsDead
	
	Page Candles
		Visible If foundCandles

		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<There's a part of
			the house that is too dark to enter without light. The candles you
			found should help. If we move fast enough, maybe we can stop
			Mathias.>>
		"""
	End Page Candles

	Page Journal
		Visible If foundJournal
		
		Text """
			Sarah looks down and notices the {c:QItemJournal}. <<The
			{c:QItemJournal}! The man who let you in was writing in it all
			week. You should read it carefully.>>
		"""
	End Page Journal

	Page Dvm
		Visible If foundDvm

		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The {c:QItemDvm} is
			a spell book. It contains many powerful spells, including rituals to
			open and close gates. Also, how to interrupt a ritual that has been
			started.
			
			<<If you cannot stop Mathias in time,
			you may need to perform a closing ritual. Closing gates is easier
			than opening them but it takes time. With the gate open, many
			horrors could come through while you are trying to close it. You
			must be prepared. Read the book carefully and read it soon.>>
		"""

		If goal == goalFeedGate Then Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The {c:QItemDVM} is
			a spell book. It contains many powerful spells, including rituals to
			open and close gates. If you cannot stop Mathias from opening a gate,
			you'll need to starve it of sacrifice.

			<<You must read the {c:QItemDvm} to better understand what is
			expected of you.>>
		"""
	End Page Dvm

	Page ElderSign
		Visible If foundElderSign

		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
			{c:QItemElderSign} is an important part of the closing ritual. It
			seals the gate permanently, meaning no gate can be opened there
			again. When the closing ritual was performed 10 years ago, 
			Uncle Peter was able to close the gate, but could not seal it.>>
		"""

		If goal == goalFeedGate Then Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
			{c:QItemElderSign} is important for their plans tonight. It is used
			to secure the gate once it is opened. Without this trinket, they
			will need a steady supply of sacrifice to keep the gate open.>>
		"""

		If goal == goalOpenGate Then Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
			{c:QItemElderSign} is a powerful protective symbol. It can be used
			to ward off evil creatures and protect people from harm. It can 
			also be used to secure a gate after it is opened. Or permanently
			seal it once it closes. It is good we found it before they did.>>
		"""
	End Page ElderSign

	Page RitualComponents
		Visible If foundRitualComponents
		
		Text """
			Sarah reaches out as if to touch the {c:QItemRitualComponents}. <<I
			recognize some of these items from the gate ritual. Both my father
			and the men who tried to stop him brought similar items to help with
			their spells and counter-spells.>>
		"""
	End Page RitualComponents

	Page Dagger
		Visible If foundDagger

		Text """
			Sarah reaches toward the {c:QItemRitualDagger}. <<I recognize this
			dagger,>> she starts. <<It looks like the one my father used ten 
			years ago. With luck, Mathias needs this but we have it.>>
		"""
	End Page Dagger

	Page Color3
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<I could feel the
			ancient one approach from the other side. Suddenly, a group of men
			broke into the altar chamber and began fighting the men Father was
			summoning. One man went to the altar, killed our father, laid
			out some materials, and spoke words I didn't understand. He closed
			the gate while his friends protected him from the men who came
			through it.>>
		"""
	End Page Color3

	Page Color4
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator},
			<<Father believed that personal sacrifice was the most powerful
			magic. For the spell he used, the gate was created by binding power 
			to the body of a loved one. Father used me to summon the gate. When
			the gate closed, I began to die slowly. The pain of the ritual so
			engulfed me that I can still feel it, 10 years on.>>
		"""
	End Page Color4
	
	Page Color5
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You found out what
			was going to happen a week before the ritual. Members of Father's
			church did something to you. After that, you followed orders
			without question. You helped Father bind me during the ritual. From
			what they said at the time, you probably cannot remember anything
			about the ritual or anything before. It's why you don't know who
			you are or remember what happened that night.>>
		"""
	End Page Color5

	Page Color6
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The day of the
			ritual, two of my friends came to visit me. When Father told them I
			wasn't allowed out, they sneaked to my window and crawled in when I
			opened it. Father was furious. I'm not sure who strangled them or
			who dragged them to the yard. I was burning alive when the gate
			closed, then my body was dumped with my friends'. It wasn't until
			then that I knew they were dead. I smoldered for several days,
			alive and conscious until the end.>>
		"""
	End Page Color6
	
	Page Color7
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<I don't know who
			the other men were, but the one who closed the gate was Uncle
			Peter---Father's brother. I think there's something special about
			our family; there are things only we can do. It's why Father could
			summon the gate, and why Uncle Peter could close it. And now Peter's
			son, our cousin Mathias, is going to try to open another gate tonight.
			
			<<You probably share the family abilities. You must trust yourself
			to know what to do.>>
		"""
	End Page Color7
	
	Page ExhortationStart
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<I am worried we are
			running out of time. You must have the {c:QItemElderSign}, 
			{c:QItemDvm}, and {c:QItemRitualComponents}. You must have also
			read {QItemDvm} and {c:QItemJournal}>>
		"""
	End Page ExhortationStart
	
	Page ExhortationJournal
		Visible If Not journalFinished
		
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<I think the
			{c:QItemJournal} has important information, things you need to know.
			You must finish reading it.
		"""
	End Page ExhortationJournal
	
	Page ExhortationDvm
		Visible If Not dvmFinished
		
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The {c:QItemDvm}
			contains infromation you must know so that you can do what needs to
			be done tonight. Please read it now. There is nothing more imporant
			that being prepared.
		"""
	End Page ExhortationDvm
	
	Page ExhortationStuff
		Visible If Not foundRitualDagger Or Not foundElderSign Or Not foundRitualComponents
		
		Text """
			Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, there are more things
			we need to find. We must continue looking through the house. Please,
			you must hurry.
		"""
		
		Mark ExhortationStart Unread
		Mark ExhortationJournal Unread
		Mark ExhortationDvm Unread
		Mark ExhortationStuff Unread
	End Page ExhortationStuff
End Book SarahPatter

